---
title = "How to append a file"
meta_title = "How to append a file in Gleam"
subtitle = "using simplifile"
description = "The simplifile package provides file system functionality that works with Gleam on both Erlang and JavaScript"
---

The `simplifile` package provides file-system functions that work on both the
Erlang and JavaScript targets. Add it as a dependency to your package:

```cli
gleam add simplifile
```

Use the [`simplfile.append`](https://simplifile.hexdocs.pm/simplifile.html#append)
function to append content to a file. If the file does not exist it will be
created, and if it does already exist then the new content will be added to the
end of any existing content.

```gleam
import simplifile.{type FileError}

pub fn record_match(winner: String, loser: String) -> Result(Nil, FileError) {
  let line = winner <> " beat " <> loser <> "\n"
  simplifile.append(to: "matches.log", contents: line)
}
```

If you want to append binary data to a file then you can use the
[`simplfile.append_bits`](https://simplifile.hexdocs.pm/simplifile.html#append_bits)
function instead.

```gleam
import simplifile

pub fn record_data(data: BitArray) -> Result(Nil, FileError) {
  simplifile.append_bits("data.bin", data)
}
```

If the file cannot be written for any reason, these functions will return a
[`simplifile.FileError`](https://simplifile.hexdocs.pm/simplifile.html#FileError).

::: alert-warning
### Files and web browsers

For security reasons web browsers do not let code directly read and write
files, so if your program runs in browser you will need to use a different
approach.

:::
